#: ../../library/numbers.rst:2
msgid ":mod:`!numbers` --- Numeric abstract base classes"
msgstr ":mod:`!numbers` --- Abstraktní základní číselné třídy"

#: ../../library/numbers.rst:7
msgid "**Source code:** :source:`Lib/numbers.py`"
msgstr "**Zdrojový kód:** :source:`Lib/numbers.py`"

#: ../../library/numbers.rst:11
msgid ""
"The :mod:`!numbers` module (:pep:`3141`) defines a hierarchy of numeric "
":term:`abstract base classes <abstract base class>` which progressively "
"define more operations.  None of the types defined in this module are "
"intended to be instantiated."
msgstr ""
"Modul :mod:`!numbers` (:pep:`3141`) definuje hierarchii numerických "
":term:`abstraktních základních tříd <abstract base class>`, které postupně "
"definují více operací. Žádný z typů definovaných v tomto modulu není určen k"
" vytváření instancí."

#: ../../library/numbers.rst:18
msgid ""
"The root of the numeric hierarchy. If you just want to check if an argument "
"*x* is a number, without caring what kind, use ``isinstance(x, Number)``."
msgstr ""
"Kořen číselné hierarchie. Pokud chcete pouze zkontrolovat, zda je argument "
"*x* číslo, bez ohledu na to, jaký druh, použijte ``isinstance(x, Number)``."

#: ../../library/numbers.rst:23
msgid "The numeric tower"
msgstr "Číselná věž"

#: ../../library/numbers.rst:27
msgid ""
"Subclasses of this type describe complex numbers and include the operations "
"that work on the built-in :class:`complex` type. These are: conversions to "
":class:`complex` and :class:`bool`, :attr:`.real`, :attr:`.imag`, ``+``, "
"``-``, ``*``, ``/``, ``**``, :func:`abs`, :meth:`conjugate`, ``==``, and "
"``!=``. All except ``-`` and ``!=`` are abstract."
msgstr ""
"Podtřídy tohoto typu popisují komplexní čísla a zahrnují operace, které "
"fungují na vestavěném typu :class:`complex`. Jedná se o: převody na "
":class:`complex` a :class:`bool`, :attr:`.real`, :attr:`.imag`, ``+``, "
"``-``, ``*``, ``/``, ``**``, :func:`abs`, :meth:`conjugate`, ``==`` a "
"``!=``. Všechny kromě ``-`` a ``!=`` jsou abstraktní."

#: ../../library/numbers.rst:35
msgid "Abstract. Retrieves the real component of this number."
msgstr "Abstraktní. Načítá skutečnou část tohoto čísla."

#: ../../library/numbers.rst:39
msgid "Abstract. Retrieves the imaginary component of this number."
msgstr "Abstraktní. Načítá imaginární část tohoto čísla."

#: ../../library/numbers.rst:44
msgid ""
"Abstract. Returns the complex conjugate. For example, ``(1+3j).conjugate() "
"== (1-3j)``."
msgstr ""
"Abstraktní. Vrací komplexní konjugát. Například ``(1+3j).conjugate() == "
"(1-3j)``."

#: ../../library/numbers.rst:49
msgid ""
"To :class:`Complex`, :class:`!Real` adds the operations that work on real "
"numbers."
msgstr ""
"K :class:`Complex` přidává :class:`!Real` operace, které fungují na reálných"
" číslech."

#: ../../library/numbers.rst:52
msgid ""
"In short, those are: a conversion to :class:`float`, :func:`math.trunc`, "
":func:`round`, :func:`math.floor`, :func:`math.ceil`, :func:`divmod`, "
"``//``, ``%``, ``<``, ``<=``, ``>``, and ``>=``."
msgstr ""
"Stručně řečeno, jedná se o: převod na :class:`float`, :func:`math.trunc`, "
":func:`round`, :func:`math.floor`, :func:`math.ceil`, :func:`divmod`, "
"``//``, ``%``, ``<``, ``<=``, ``>`` a ``>=``."

#: ../../library/numbers.rst:56
msgid ""
"Real also provides defaults for :func:`complex`, :attr:`~Complex.real`, "
":attr:`~Complex.imag`, and :meth:`~Complex.conjugate`."
msgstr ""
":class:`Real` také poskytuje výchozí hodnoty pro :func:`complex`, "
":attr:`~Complex.real`, :attr:`~Complex.imag` a :meth:`~Complex.conjugate`."

#: ../../library/numbers.rst:62
msgid ""
"Subtypes :class:`Real` and adds :attr:`~Rational.numerator` and "
":attr:`~Rational.denominator` properties. It also provides a default for "
":func:`float`."
msgstr ""
"Rozdělí :class:`Real` a přidá :attr:`~Rational.numerator` a "
":attr:`~Rational.denominator` vlastnosti. Poskytuje také výchozí hodnotu pro"
" :func:`float`."

#: ../../library/numbers.rst:66
msgid ""
"The :attr:`~Rational.numerator` and :attr:`~Rational.denominator` values "
"should be instances of :class:`Integral` and should be in lowest terms with "
":attr:`~Rational.denominator` positive."
msgstr ""
"Hodnoty :attr:`~Rational.numerator` a :attr:`~Rational.denominator` by měly "
"být instancemi :class:`Integral` a měly by být v nejnižších termínech s "
":attr:`~Rational.denominator` kladné."

#: ../../library/numbers.rst:72
msgid "Abstract.  The numerator of this rational number."
msgstr "Abstraktní. Číslené tohoto racionálního čísla."

#: ../../library/numbers.rst:76
msgid "Abstract.  The denominator of this rational number."
msgstr "Abstraktní. Jmenovatel tohoto racionálního čísla."

#: ../../library/numbers.rst:81
msgid ""
"Subtypes :class:`Rational` and adds a conversion to :class:`int`.  Provides "
"defaults for :func:`float`, :attr:`~Rational.numerator`, and "
":attr:`~Rational.denominator`.  Adds abstract methods for :func:`pow` with "
"modulus and bit-string operations: ``<<``, ``>>``, ``&``, ``^``, ``|``, "
"``~``."
msgstr ""
"Rozdělí :class:`Rational` a přidá převod na :class:`int`. Poskytuje výchozí "
"hodnoty pro :func:`float`, :attr:`~Rational.numerator` a "
":attr:`~Rational.denominator`. Přidává abstraktní metody pro :func:`pow` s "
"modulárem a operace bitového řetězce: ``<<``, ``>>``, ``&``, ``^``, ``|``, "
"``~``."

#: ../../library/numbers.rst:89
msgid "Notes for type implementers"
msgstr "Poznámky pro implementátory typů"

#: ../../library/numbers.rst:91
msgid ""
"Implementers should be careful to make equal numbers equal and hash them to "
"the same values. This may be subtle if there are two different extensions of"
" the real numbers. For example, :class:`fractions.Fraction` implements "
":func:`hash` as follows::"
msgstr ""
"Implementátoři by měli být opatrní, aby zajistili, že stejná čísla jsou "
"součástí stejné třídy a jsou zahashována na stejné hodnoty. To může být "
"zdélavé, pokud existují dvě různé rozšíření reálných čísel. Například "
":class:`fractions.Fraction` implementuje :func:`hash` takto::"

#: ../../library/numbers.rst:96
msgid ""
"def __hash__(self):\n"
"    if self.denominator == 1:\n"
"        # Get integers right.\n"
"        return hash(self.numerator)\n"
"    # Expensive check, but definitely correct.\n"
"    if self == float(self):\n"
"        return hash(float(self))\n"
"    else:\n"
"        # Use tuple's hash to avoid a high collision rate on\n"
"        # simple fractions.\n"
"        return hash((self.numerator, self.denominator))"
msgstr ""
"def __hash__(self):\n"
"    if self.denominator == 1:\n"
"        # Get integers right.\n"
"        return hash(self.numerator)\n"
"    # Expensive check, but definitely correct.\n"
"    if self == float(self):\n"
"        return hash(float(self))\n"
"    else:\n"
"        # Use tuple's hash to avoid a high collision rate on\n"
"        # simple fractions.\n"
"        return hash((self.numerator, self.denominator))"

#: ../../library/numbers.rst:110
msgid "Adding More Numeric ABCs"
msgstr "Přidání dalších numerických ABC"

#: ../../library/numbers.rst:112
msgid ""
"There are, of course, more possible ABCs for numbers, and this would be a "
"poor hierarchy if it precluded the possibility of adding those. You can add "
"``MyFoo`` between :class:`Complex` and :class:`Real` with::"
msgstr ""
"Samozřejmě existují další možné ABC pro čísla a tato hierarchie by byla "
"špatná, kdyby vyloučila možnost jejich přidání. Můžete přidat ``MyFoo`` mezi"
" :class:`Complex` a :class:`Real` takto::"

#: ../../library/numbers.rst:117
msgid ""
"class MyFoo(Complex): ...\n"
"MyFoo.register(Real)"
msgstr ""
"class MyFoo(Complex): ...\n"
"MyFoo.register(Real)"

#: ../../library/numbers.rst:124
msgid "Implementing the arithmetic operations"
msgstr "Implementace aritmetických operací"

#: ../../library/numbers.rst:126
msgid ""
"We want to implement the arithmetic operations so that mixed-mode operations"
" either call an implementation whose author knew about the types of both "
"arguments, or convert both to the nearest built in type and do the operation"
" there. For subtypes of :class:`Integral`, this means that "
":meth:`~object.__add__` and :meth:`~object.__radd__` should be defined as::"
msgstr ""
"Chceme implementovat aritmetické operace tak, aby smíšené operace bud' "
"volaly implementaci, jejíž autor znal typy obou argumentů, nebo převedli oba"
" na nejbližší vestavěný typ a provedly operaci tam. Pro podtypy "
":class:`Integral` to znamená, že :meth:`~object.__add__` a "
":meth:`~object.__radd__` by měly být definovány takto::"

#: ../../library/numbers.rst:133
msgid ""
"class MyIntegral(Integral):\n"
"\n"
"    def __add__(self, other):\n"
"        if isinstance(other, MyIntegral):\n"
"            return do_my_adding_stuff(self, other)\n"
"        elif isinstance(other, OtherTypeIKnowAbout):\n"
"            return do_my_other_adding_stuff(self, other)\n"
"        else:\n"
"            return NotImplemented\n"
"\n"
"    def __radd__(self, other):\n"
"        if isinstance(other, MyIntegral):\n"
"            return do_my_adding_stuff(other, self)\n"
"        elif isinstance(other, OtherTypeIKnowAbout):\n"
"            return do_my_other_adding_stuff(other, self)\n"
"        elif isinstance(other, Integral):\n"
"            return int(other) + int(self)\n"
"        elif isinstance(other, Real):\n"
"            return float(other) + float(self)\n"
"        elif isinstance(other, Complex):\n"
"            return complex(other) + complex(self)\n"
"        else:\n"
"            return NotImplemented"
msgstr ""
"class MyIntegral(Integral):\n"
"\n"
"    def __add__(self, other):\n"
"        if isinstance(other, MyIntegral):\n"
"            return do_my_adding_stuff(self, other)\n"
"        elif isinstance(other, OtherTypeIKnowAbout):\n"
"            return do_my_other_adding_stuff(self, other)\n"
"        else:\n"
"            return NotImplemented\n"
"\n"
"    def __radd__(self, other):\n"
"        if isinstance(other, MyIntegral):\n"
"            return do_my_adding_stuff(other, self)\n"
"        elif isinstance(other, OtherTypeIKnowAbout):\n"
"            return do_my_other_adding_stuff(other, self)\n"
"        elif isinstance(other, Integral):\n"
"            return int(other) + int(self)\n"
"        elif isinstance(other, Real):\n"
"            return float(other) + float(self)\n"
"        elif isinstance(other, Complex):\n"
"            return complex(other) + complex(self)\n"
"        else:\n"
"            return NotImplemented"

#: ../../library/numbers.rst:158
msgid ""
"There are 5 different cases for a mixed-type operation on subclasses of "
":class:`Complex`. I'll refer to all of the above code that doesn't refer to "
"``MyIntegral`` and ``OtherTypeIKnowAbout`` as \"boilerplate\". ``a`` will be"
" an instance of ``A``, which is a subtype of :class:`Complex` (``a : A <: "
"Complex``), and ``b : B <: Complex``. I'll consider ``a + b``:"
msgstr ""
"Existují 4 různé případy pro smíšenou operaci na podtypech :class:`Complex`."
" Budu odkazovat na všechny výše uvedené kódy, které se nevztahují na "
"``MyIntegral`` a ``OtherTypeIKnowAbout``, jako na \"vzor\". ``a`` bude "
"instancí ``A``, což je podtyp :class:`Complex` (``a : A <: Complex``), a ``b"
" : B <: Complex``. Zvažuji ``a + b``:"

#: ../../library/numbers.rst:165
msgid ""
"If ``A`` defines an :meth:`~object.__add__` which accepts ``b``, all is "
"well."
msgstr ""
"Pokud ``A`` definuje :meth:`~object.__add__`, který přijímá ``b``, vše je v "
"pořádku."

#: ../../library/numbers.rst:167
msgid ""
"If ``A`` falls back to the boilerplate code, and it were to return a value "
"from :meth:`~object.__add__`, we'd miss the possibility that ``B`` defines a"
" more intelligent :meth:`~object.__radd__`, so the boilerplate should return"
" :data:`NotImplemented` from :meth:`!__add__`. (Or ``A`` may not implement "
":meth:`!__add__` at all.)"
msgstr ""
"Pokud se ``A`` vrátí k vzoru kódu a vrátí hodnotu z :meth:`~object.__add__`,"
" promine zmožnost, že ``B`` definuje inteligentnější "
":meth:`~object.__radd__`, takže by vzor kódu měl vrátit "
":data:`NotImplemented` z :meth:`!__add__`. (Nebo ``A`` nemusí implementovat "
":meth:`!__add__` vůbec.)"

#: ../../library/numbers.rst:173
msgid ""
"Then ``B``'s :meth:`~object.__radd__` gets a chance. If it accepts ``a``, "
"all is well."
msgstr ""
"Pak :meth:`~object.__radd__` z ``B`` získá šanci. Pokud přijímá ``a``, vše "
"je v pořádku."

#: ../../library/numbers.rst:175
msgid ""
"If it falls back to the boilerplate, there are no more possible methods to "
"try, so this is where the default implementation should live."
msgstr ""
"Pokud se vrátí k vzoru kódu, neexistují žádné další možné metody k pokusu, "
"takže toto je místo, kde by měla žít výchozí implementace."

#: ../../library/numbers.rst:178
msgid ""
"If ``B <: A``, Python tries ``B.__radd__`` before ``A.__add__``. This is ok,"
" because it was implemented with knowledge of ``A``, so it can handle those "
"instances before delegating to :class:`Complex`."
msgstr ""
"Pokud se ``B <: A``, Python zkusí ``B.__radd__`` před ``A.__add__``. To je "
"ok, protože byla implementována se znalostem ``A``, takže může zpracovat ty "
"instance před delegováním na :class:`Complex`."

#: ../../library/numbers.rst:183
msgid ""
"If ``A <: Complex`` and ``B <: Real`` without sharing any other knowledge, "
"then the appropriate shared operation is the one involving the built in "
":class:`complex`, and both :meth:`~object.__radd__` s land there, so ``a+b "
"== b+a``."
msgstr ""
"Pokud ``A <: Complex`` a ``B <: Real`` bez sdíleého znáení, pak odpovíjající"
" sdíenou operací je ta, která zahrnuje vestavěné :class:`complex`, a oba "
":meth:`~object.__radd__` se tam vyskytují, takže ``a+b == b+a``."

#: ../../library/numbers.rst:188
msgid ""
"Because most of the operations on any given type will be very similar, it "
"can be useful to define a helper function which generates the forward and "
"reverse instances of any given operator. For example, "
":class:`fractions.Fraction` uses::"
msgstr ""
"Protože vétšina operací na jakémkoli typem budou velmi podobné, může být "
"užitečné definovat funkční funkci, která generuje před a zpětné instance "
"jakéhokoli operátoru. Například :class:`fractions.Fraction` používá::"

#: ../../library/numbers.rst:193
msgid ""
"def _operator_fallbacks(monomorphic_operator, fallback_operator):\n"
"    def forward(a, b):\n"
"        if isinstance(b, (int, Fraction)):\n"
"            return monomorphic_operator(a, b)\n"
"        elif isinstance(b, float):\n"
"            return fallback_operator(float(a), b)\n"
"        elif isinstance(b, complex):\n"
"            return fallback_operator(complex(a), b)\n"
"        else:\n"
"            return NotImplemented\n"
"    forward.__name__ = '__' + fallback_operator.__name__ + '__'\n"
"    forward.__doc__ = monomorphic_operator.__doc__\n"
"\n"
"    def reverse(b, a):\n"
"        if isinstance(a, Rational):\n"
"            # Includes ints.\n"
"            return monomorphic_operator(a, b)\n"
"        elif isinstance(a, Real):\n"
"            return fallback_operator(float(a), float(b))\n"
"        elif isinstance(a, Complex):\n"
"            return fallback_operator(complex(a), complex(b))\n"
"        else:\n"
"            return NotImplemented\n"
"    reverse.__name__ = '__r' + fallback_operator.__name__ + '__'\n"
"    reverse.__doc__ = monomorphic_operator.__doc__\n"
"\n"
"    return forward, reverse\n"
"\n"
"def _add(a, b):\n"
"    \"\"\"a + b\"\"\"\n"
"    return Fraction(a.numerator * b.denominator +\n"
"                    b.numerator * a.denominator,\n"
"                    a.denominator * b.denominator)\n"
"\n"
"__add__, __radd__ = _operator_fallbacks(_add, operator.add)\n"
"\n"
"# ..."
msgstr ""
"def _operator_fallbacks(monomorphic_operator, fallback_operator):\n"
"    def forward(a, b):\n"
"        if isinstance(b, (int, Fraction)):\n"
"            return monomorphic_operator(a, b)\n"
"        elif isinstance(b, float):\n"
"            return fallback_operator(float(a), b)\n"
"        elif isinstance(b, complex):\n"
"            return fallback_operator(complex(a), b)\n"
"        else:\n"
"            return NotImplemented\n"
"    forward.__name__ = '__' + fallback_operator.__name__ + '__'\n"
"    forward.__doc__ = monomorphic_operator.__doc__\n"
"\n"
"    def reverse(b, a):\n"
"        if isinstance(a, Rational):\n"
"            # Includes ints.\n"
"            return monomorphic_operator(a, b)\n"
"        elif isinstance(a, Real):\n"
"            return fallback_operator(float(a), float(b))\n"
"        elif isinstance(a, Complex):\n"
"            return fallback_operator(complex(a), complex(b))\n"
"        else:\n"
"            return NotImplemented\n"
"    reverse.__name__ = '__r' + fallback_operator.__name__ + '__'\n"
"    reverse.__doc__ = monomorphic_operator.__doc__\n"
"\n"
"    return forward, reverse\n"
"\n"
"def _add(a, b):\n"
"    \"\"\"a + b\"\"\"\n"
"    return Fraction(a.numerator * b.denominator +\n"
"                    b.numerator * a.denominator,\n"
"                    a.denominator * b.denominator)\n"
"\n"
"__add__, __radd__ = _operator_fallbacks(_add, operator.add)\n"
"\n"
"# ..."
